WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.820
Dashboards turn telemetry into a shared operating picture.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.120
They should be designed for decisions, not decoration.

3
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:21.820
A useful dashboard connects system health to workflow purpose: whether the AI service is available, whether requests are succeeding, whether latency is acceptable, whether retrieval is healthy, and whether resource pressure is changing.

4
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.620
Different audiences may need different views.

5
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:31.800
Operators may focus on service health, queue depth, model loading, hardware pressure, and failures.

6
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:40.620
Privacy and governance reviewers may focus on logging modes, audit exceptions, retention status, export activity, and access patterns.

7
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:48.320
Engineering leads may watch usage trends, cost signals, backlog items, and recurring reliability problems.

8
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.080
A dashboard is only the start.

9
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.620
Operational reviews turn data into action.

10
00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:08.240
A weekly or monthly review might identify stale debug logging, repeated failures in a connector, a model server that needs tuning, a workflow with unclear ownership, or retention rules that no longer match policy.

11
00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.700
The outcome should be notes, backlog items, owners, and follow-up dates.

12
00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.780
Trends often matter more than isolated numbers.

13
00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:26.160
A single slow request may be unimportant, while a steady rise in latency, storage use, queue depth, or audit exceptions may reveal a larger issue.

14
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:30.580
Reviews help teams see gradual drift before it becomes an incident.

15
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.540
Good review habits make sovereign AI operations more accountable.

16
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:43.120
They connect telemetry to maintenance, privacy, governance, and continuous improvement instead of leaving metrics to sit unread.
